# The machine deploy/deploy.sh deploys to, deploy/launch-setup.sh hardens, and
# deploy/backup/pull-backups.sh copies database snapshots from.
#
#     cp deploy/deploy.env.example deploy/deploy.env      # then fill in the values
#
# deploy.env is gitignored; this example is not, and must never name a real host.
# A variable already set in the environment wins over this file.

# --- how the host runs the site ---

# systemd (the default): a systemd unit runs the server from server/.venv, and the
# host's nginx serves the website from DEPLOY_WEB_ROOT. launch-setup.sh sets up
# only this kind of host.
# docker: docker-compose.yml in DEPLOY_REPO runs the server, nginx and the nightly
# snapshots (README.md, "Deploy on a clean VM with Docker"). Then:
#   DEPLOY_HOST       the SSH user must be in the `docker` group, and needs no sudo
#   DEPLOY_REPO       the VM's PatchingSite clone, which holds .env
#   DEPLOY_WEB_ROOT   unused: the website is built into the web image
#   DEPLOY_STORE_APK  $HOST_PATCHED_DIR/store.apk on the VM, HOST_PATCHED_DIR from .env
# DEPLOY_RUNTIME=systemd

# --- required ---

# The SSH login. Key-based (the scripts never prompt), with passwordless sudo for
# systemctl, and able to `git fetch` this repository.
DEPLOY_HOST=deploy@example.com

# The host's checkout of this repository, with server/.venv already set up.
DEPLOY_REPO=/home/deploy/PatchingSite

# systemd only: where nginx serves the website from. Outside the SSH user's home,
# which nginx cannot read; deploy.sh copies each build here.
DEPLOY_WEB_ROOT=/var/www/example.com

# The public address. deploy.sh checks /api/health through it after a restart, as
# a user would reach it; launch-setup.sh names the TLS certificate after its host.
DEPLOY_SITE_URL=https://example.com

# --- optional: defaults match server/config.py and deploy/patchingsite.service ---

# Where the store app is published (the server's STORE_APK_PATH).
# DEPLOY_STORE_APK=/opt/patched/store.apk

# The systemd unit running the server.
# DEPLOY_SERVICE=patchingsite

# The commit each component was last deployed at. A relative path is under the SSH
# user's home.
# DEPLOY_STATE_DIR=.deploy-state

# Where this machine keeps each published store build's R8 mapping, which is the
# only way to decode its crash reports. Defaults to ~/.local/share/androidmod/mappings.
# DEPLOY_MAPPING_DIR=

# launch-setup.sh only: the mail settings it adds to the host's .env once. The
# sending account, the support address users see (defaults to the sender), and a
# file on this machine holding the account's app password, which is sent over
# stdin and never stored in the repo. Give the file as an absolute path.
# SMTP_USERNAME=
# SUPPORT_EMAIL=
# SMTP_PASSWORD_FILE=           # defaults to ~/.config/androidmod/smtp-app-password

# pull-backups.sh only. BACKUP_HOST defaults to DEPLOY_HOST.
# BACKUP_HOST=
# BACKUP_REMOTE_DIR=/var/lib/patchingsite-backups
# BACKUP_LOCAL_DIR=           # defaults to ~/Backups/androidmod
# BACKUP_KEEP=60
